# {{project-name}}

{{description}}

A [witmproxy](https://witmproxy.rs) plugin, compiled to a signed WASM component.

## Build

```sh
make
```

This generates a signing keypair on first run (`key.secret` / `key.public`),
builds for `wasm32-wasip2`, and signs the component. The public key is compiled
into the component itself, and the host verifies the signature against it before
loading the plugin -- so rebuild after any key change.

Prerequisites:

```sh
rustup target add wasm32-wasip2
cargo install wasmsign2-cli
```

## Install

```sh
witm plugin add target/wasm32-wasip2/release/{{crate_name}}.signed.wasm
```

## Where to start

* `manifest()` in `src/lib.rs` declares the plugin's identity and the
  capabilities it requests. The user decides what is actually granted and may
  narrow any scope, so treat every capability as optional.
* `handle()` in `src/lib.rs` is the event handler.

Each requested capability carries a CEL `scope` expression that the host
evaluates *before* instantiating this component. Narrow scopes are not just a
permissions story -- they let the host skip instantiation entirely for events
you do not care about, which is the cheapest performance win available to you.

## WIT

`wit/` is vendored from the host at generation time, so it matches the witmproxy
version that generated this project ({{witm-version}}). To move to a newer host:

```sh
wkg get --format wit witmproxy:plugin@<version> --output wit/world.wit
```

